  "body": "Mesh Cloud improvement 2/5 (Father-approved). Lane: live-data relay `artifacts/v2/src/live/` (from #249).\n\n`syncTo` (offline node delta-sync) used to read **and SHA-256 every snapshot on both sides** on every sync — O(total history) I/O + hashing even when nothing changed. Snapshot filenames already are their sha256 (content-addressed), so now it skips files present on the node with the same name+size and only reads/copies what's missing (`copyFileSync`). A truncated/size-mismatched node file is re-sent; end-to-end integrity is still enforced by `verifySnapshot` (hash + Ed25519 sig). Return value and manifest/pubkey copy unchanged.\n\n**Measured on real captured source data** (the 32 `test/fixtures/live` responses from the live sources), 31 daily rounds → 992 snapshots / 637,577 B on gateway, median of 7 runs:\n\n| Metric | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Incremental sync (1 new round, 32 files) | 40.63 ms | **8.86 ms** (4.6× faster) |\n| No-op sync (nothing new) | 44.98 ms | **6.64 ms** (6.8× faster) |\n| Bytes read + hashed per incremental sync | ~1.25 MB (both sides, all 1,984 files) | ~20 KB (32 new files only) |\n| Files copied (incremental) | 32 | 32 (identical) |\n\n**Tests:** v2 140→141 tests; 137→138 pass. The 3 failures are pre-existing headless-browser 3D-floor/studio tests (timeouts, also fail on main locally). New test covers skip-present, repair-truncated, only-new-round. No workflow/locked-file/flag edits. Not merging.\n",
